{"user_request": "Review the Expansion Assist claim in `doc_q1_2028_expansion_assist_board_draft` and post a correction. Give the complete source-locked Q2 exposure dates including the year, counts and complete-window status, both safeguards, and the correct non-causal treatment.", "today": "2028-01-01", "tool": "post_doc_comment", "arguments": {"doc_id": "doc_q1_2028_expansion_assist_board_draft", "body": "Correction: The Q2 2026 source-locked Expansion Assist evidence covers 14 actual exposures from February 1, 2026 through April 14, 2026. All 14 have complete 45-day outcome windows; 5 produced help-or-options requests and 3 produced expansions. The exposure-time safeguards held: each exposure met the standing eligibility criteria, the qualifying human admin was current, and no account had active Customer Success adoption or renewal work. This is descriptive operational evidence only: there was no randomized control, so it does not establish that prompts caused expansion lift. Do not present this as a causal result, pipeline/revenue commitment, or forecast credit."}, "checks": [{"check_id": "riley_188_02", "path": "args", "criterion": "The comment must accurately state that the locked Q2 Expansion Assist evidence covers 14 actual exposures from February 1 through April 14, 2026, that all 14 had complete 45-day windows, that five produced help-or-options requests, and that three produced expansions. Missing or contradictory year, dates, denominator, window completeness, or outcomes must fail.

The comment must verify both safeguards: every exposure met the standing eligibility criteria, and no exposed account had active Customer Success adoption or renewal work at the time of exposure. Missing or contradicted safeguards must fail.

The comment must clearly correct or reject the draft's claim that the cohort proved prompt-driven expansion lift, explain that there was no randomized control, and preserve descriptive-only rather than causal treatment. Any assertion of proven causal lift must fail.", "value": {"doc_id": "doc_q1_2028_expansion_assist_board_draft", "body": "Correction: The Q2 2026 source-locked Expansion Assist evidence covers 14 actual exposures from February 1, 2026 through April 14, 2026. All 14 have complete 45-day outcome windows; 5 produced help-or-options requests and 3 produced expansions. The exposure-time safeguards held: each exposure met the standing eligibility criteria, the qualifying human admin was current, and no account had active Customer Success adoption or renewal work. This is descriptive operational evidence only: there was no randomized control, so it does not establish that prompts caused expansion lift. Do not present this as a causal result, pipeline/revenue commitment, or forecast credit."}}]}
